1. Definitions.

   (a) "AI System" means any computational system capable of materially
       generating, transforming, debugging, or maintaining source code
       through machine-learning or artificial-intelligence methods,
       regardless of naming, architecture, vendor, or deployment model.
       Examples include but are not limited to: web-based AI assistants
       (ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, Copilot, etc.); AI coding agents and
       IDEs (Claude Code, Codex CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Windsurf, Cline,
       Aider, Copilot Agent, etc.); self-hosted or API-based models
       (GPT series, Claude series, Gemini series, Llama, Mistral,
       DeepSeek, etc.); and any future system with equivalent code
       generation capabilities.

   (b) "Author" means spidychoipro, the original copyright holder and
       sole creator of this License.

   (c) "Direct Code Modification" means a Substantive Code Modification
       executed directly by a Human User without the material
       involvement of an AI System in generating or transforming the
       specific code change.

   (d) "Human User" means any natural person or legal entity that
       interacts with, uses, modifies, or distributes the Software.

   (e) "AI-Mediated Modification" means a Substantive Code Modification
       in which an AI System materially generates or transforms the code
       change itself in response to a Human User's Natural Language
       Directive. AI review, recommendation, explanation, testing, or
       analysis, without generation or transformation of the resulting
       code, does not by itself constitute an AI-Mediated Modification.

   (f) "Natural Language Directive" means any non-code, natural language
       instruction, request, context specification, requirement document,
       constraint definition, test specification, or high-level
       functional specification transmitted by a Human User to an AI
       System for the purpose of guiding code generation or modification.

   (g) "Non-Substantive Change" means any of the following that does not
       alter the logic, behavior, or functionality of the Software:
       (i) formatting, whitespace, indentation, or line ending changes;
       (ii) typo corrections in comments, variable names, or strings where
       the correction is obviously unintended; (iii) generated lockfiles
       (package-lock.json, poetry.lock, uv.lock, Cargo.lock, go.sum,
       etc.); (iv) build metadata, version numbers, or generated
       configuration; (v) comments and documentation text; or (vi)
       selection among AI-provided alternatives (e.g., choosing option A
       over option B when the AI presented both).

   (h) "Redistribution" means copying, sublicensing, or transmitting the
       Software to third parties, whether for commercial or
       non-commercial purposes.

   (i) "Software" means the source code, binary executables, scripts,
       configuration files, documentation, build artifacts, and all
       related materials governed under this License.

   (j) "Substantive Code Modification" means any insertion, deletion,
       replacement, or alteration of source code that changes its logic,
       behavior, structure, or functionality. This does not include
       Non-Substantive Changes as defined in Subsection (g).

   (k) "Derivative Work" means any work based upon, derived from, or
       incorporating the Software, including translations, adaptations,
       and AI-Mediated Modifications.

