       (i) use, run, execute, and interact with the Software for any
       purpose, commercial or non-commercial; (ii) study, inspect,
       analyze, and reverse-engineer the Software source code for
       educational, research, or verification purposes; (iii) create and
       distribute unmodified copies of the Software; (iv) create and
       distribute AI-Mediated Modifications of the Software, provided
       such modifications comply with Section 3; and (v) sublicense the
       rights granted under this Section to third parties, provided all
       recipients are bound by this License.

   (b) Modification Right. The right to create Substantive Code
       Modifications of the Software may be exercised only through an AI
       System. A Human User may formulate Natural Language Directives,
       specifications, constraints, and tests, but may not directly alter
       the substantive source code.

   (c) All rights not expressly granted under this License are reserved
       by the Author.

3. Workflow: AI-Mediated Modification.

   (a) The intended workflow for modifying the Software is as follows:
       Step 1: The Human User formulates a Natural Language Directive
       describing what change is needed and why. Step 2: The AI System
       receives the directive and generates or transforms the source code
       accordingly. Step 3: The Human User reviews the AI-Mediated
       Modification, validates the result, and accepts or requests
       further changes. In summary: the Human User decides WHAT to change
       and WHY; the AI System determines HOW to change the code; the
       Human User reviews and accepts the result.

   (b) A Human User shall not perform Direct Code Modification of the
       Software. All Substantive Code Modifications must be AI-Mediated
       Modifications as defined in Subsection 1(e).

   (c) Anti-Circumvention (Source Code). A Human User shall not
       circumvent this License by manually introducing externally
       authored source code and merely requesting an AI System to insert,
       reproduce, or reformat that code. The AI System must materially
       generate or transform the code, not merely relay it.

   (d) Anti-Circumvention (Compiled Artifacts). A Human User shall not
       circumvent the AI-Mediated Modification requirement by directly
       modifying compiled binaries, generated artifacts, bytecode, or
       other executable representations where such modification is
       functionally equivalent to a Substantive Code Modification. This
       restriction does not prohibit ordinary compilation, linking,
       packaging, optimization, or other automated build processes
       performed from compliant source code.

   (e) Human authorship of a Natural Language Directive, specification,
       requirement, or design document does not, by itself, constitute
       Direct Code Modification.

   (f) This workflow requirement does not apply to Non-Substantive
       Changes as defined in Subsection 1(g).

4. Permitted Human User Activities.

   (a) Human Users are permitted to:
       (i) provide Natural Language Directives to AI Systems for the
       purpose of generating AI-Mediated Modifications; (ii) execute,
       build, test, run, and deploy the Software; (iii) report bugs,
       issues, feature requests, or desired behaviors; (iv) fork, clone,
       and redistribute the Software, subject to the terms of this
       License; (v) use the Software for personal, educational, research,
       commercial, or any other purpose; (vi) provide qualitative
       feedback, log output, or runtime behavior reports for debugging
       purposes; (vii) make Non-Substantive Changes as defined in
       Subsection 1(g); and (viii) apply emergency patches for critical
       security vulnerabilities when an AI System is not immediately
       available, provided that the patch is regenerated through an AI
       System within a reasonable period after an AI System becomes
       available (see Subsection 5.6).

   (b) Human Users are solely responsible for:
       (i) selecting appropriate and trustworthy AI Systems for code
       modification; (ii) reviewing, auditing, and validating all
       AI-Mediated Modifications before deployment or distribution;
       (iii) ensuring that AI-Mediated Modifications do not infringe upon
       third-party intellectual property rights, privacy laws, or
       applicable regulations; (iv) all consequences, damages, or losses
       arising from the use, deployment, or distribution of AI-Mediated
       Modifications in any environment, including production systems;
       (v) maintaining adequate backups, version control, and rollback
       capabilities for all AI-Mediated Modifications; and (vi)
       conducting security audits and quality assurance on any
       AI-Mediated Modifications prior to production deployment.

5. User Responsibility and Assumption of Risk.

   (a) AI may generate the code. AI does not assume legal responsibility
       for the code. The Human User assumes all responsibility.

   (b) THE HUMAN USER ACKNOWLEDGES AND AGREES that they bear sole and
       complete responsibility for the use, modification, and
       distribution of the Software and any AI-Mediated Modifications
       thereof. The Author shall not be held liable for any damages,
       defects, security vulnerabilities, data loss, system failures,
       business interruption, or any other consequences resulting from
       the use or modification of the Software.

   (c) THE HUMAN USER acknowledges that AI Systems may produce code
       containing errors, security flaws, unintended behavior,
       hallucinated implementations, outdated dependencies, or
       non-terminating execution paths. The Human User is responsible for
       thoroughly reviewing, testing, and validating all AI-Mediated
       Modifications prior to use in any environment, especially
       production or safety-critical systems.

   (d) THE HUMAN USER shall be responsible for, and shall not hold the
       Author liable for, any claims, damages, losses, liabilities,
       costs, and expenses arising from or relating to the Human User's
       use, modification, or redistribution of the Software, including
       but not limited to AI-Mediated Modifications.

   (e) No warranty is made that AI-Mediated Modifications will be
       accurate, complete, secure, performant, or free of defects. The
       Human User must perform independent verification, code review,
       and quality assurance appropriate to their specific use case and
       risk tolerance.

   (f) Emergency Exception. In the event of a critical security
       vulnerability or catastrophic bug where an AI System is not
       immediately available, a Human User may apply a temporary direct
       patch. However, the Human User must regenerate the patch through
       an AI System within a reasonable period after an AI System becomes
       available for use, and must document the emergency modification.
       Failure to do so may be considered a license violation.

6. AI Modification Record (Recommended).

   (a) This Section is a recommendation, not a requirement. Compliance
       with this License does not depend on maintaining an AI
       Modification Record.

   (b) The Author recommends that projects using this License maintain
       an AI Modification Record to document the provenance of changes. A
       suggested format is:

       .aiopl/
           modifications/
               2026-09-02-001.json

       {
           "license": "AI-OPL-1.2",
           "agent": "Claude Code",
           "files": ["src/main.py", "src/utils.py"],
           "human_directive": "Refactor the parser and add error handling",
           "timestamp": "2026-09-02T22:40:00+09:00"
       }

       The record MAY omit or redact confidential, personal,
       security-sensitive, or proprietary information.

   (c) The Author further recommends that commits containing AI-Mediated
       Modifications include a trailer such as:

       Co-authored-by: <AI System Name>

       or a similar marker to indicate AI involvement in the change.

   (d) These records are advisory only and do not create legal
       obligations. They exist to support transparency and to help
       establish a culture of AI-aware development practices.

